<p class="sub-head"><a name="Common_operations_with_project_files"></a>Common operations with project files</p>
<table width="811" cellspacing="0" class="whs19">
<col class="whs20">
<col class="whs21">
<col class="whs22">
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="16.852%" class="whs24">
<p class="caption">Command</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="74.64%" class="whs25">
<p class="caption">Description</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="4.125%" class="whs26">
<p class="caption">Details</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="16.852%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">New</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="74.64%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Standard Windows command to create new file. In KUBE it will be an empty document, named Scan DataXX, where XX stands for a number.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="4.125%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/New.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="16.852%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Open</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="74.64%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Standard Windows command to open an existing file. In KUBE can be loaded files with different file extensions (.sab2, .tri, .stl, etc).</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="4.125%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Open.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="16.852%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func">Open in Current Document</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="74.64%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Standard Windows command to open an existing file and load it in the current document. In KUBE can be loaded files with different file extensions (.sab2, .tri, .stl, etc).</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="4.125%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Open_in_Current_Document.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="16.852%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Close</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="74.64%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Standard Windows command to close the currently opened file.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="4.125%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/close.htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="16.852%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Save</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="74.64%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Standard Windows command to save the current file. In KUBE : if it is a new file (not preliminary saved), you will be prompted for a name and the document will be saved with sab2 extension.</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="4.125%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Save_(As).htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs23">
<td width="16.852%" class="whs27">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span class="Command">Save As</span></p>
</td>
<td width="74.64%" class="whs28">
<p class="normal-table">Standard Windows command to save the current file with a different name.</p>
</td>
<td width="4.125%" class="whs29">
<p class="normal-table"><a href="../References/Save_(As).htm"><img src="../Corrosion/Images/i_blue_sm.jpg" width="23px" height="16px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></a></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
